{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04AD", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4cbf5e3ff6c2c34d2715d7d4a6c9fe70259a4de962b716ed2e9f7f2596667c6f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is Mumford's definition of a geometric quotient (at least the definition\nfrom the first edition of GIT; as far as we can tell later editions\nchanged ``universally submersive'' to ``submersive'').\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e063d2e32f1a9e68981fe18f0e6e93d68d58e3b4e249a271425533070f7b4bb9", "unit_id": "tag:04AD:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04AD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0008": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$R$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{item-submersive}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-geometric}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5a94865c5d93d8e8e34152cb04d7d137889c31c3a3312c6df5fb3522abd1da05", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:afe400036296d4e9e2bdaf3145ef04c4cfba3e7fef044c3a2c9ec3c9cec18ced", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme and <MATH_0002> an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation.\nA morphism <MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nis called a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>geometric quotient<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0007> is an orbit space,\n<STRUCT_0003> condition (<REF_0001>) holds universally, i.e.,\n<MATH_0008> is universally submersive, and\n<STRUCT_0004> the functions on <MATH_0009> are the <MATH_0010>-invariant functions on <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:16072f5394fff01fc3b5192e3ec94ef285f8e3500a8b0377f1a78ba6e4d3bc8a", "unit_id": "tag:04AE:statement"}
